    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="1228" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1032"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.6362/7–3045</note>
                <head>No. 1050<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of the British
                        Embassy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Miles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Assistant Adviser on German Economic Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >deWilde</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Ref. G269/–/45</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-30">July 30, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear deWilde</hi>, I enclose an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Aide-Mémoire</hi> relating to the draft directive on coal production in
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>Presumably you will be hearing from Potsdam yourself about the discussions that
                    have taken place there. I do not know whether you consider any further
                    coordination is necessary over the timing of the two directives.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard
                                Miles</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1050-a1.xml" xpointer="d1050-a1"/>
            </div>
